</div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by portalling into the material world, seeing as the Dreaming Roads are only mechanically in the Hedge in the sense that that's how you get there and there's no Mask, but Page 222 of the corebook mentions what happens if an oneiropomp gets dropped into the material world by a collapsing Bastion.<br /> <br /> If they were in dream form, they're in Twilight, which definitionally means they cannot be seen, and they then must make their way back to their body before they can roll to wake up like they would normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T19:27:07-07:00","id":1537846,"title":"","content":"CTL 2e p. 222 describes a scenario where a changeling in dream form who can't escape a dream before it collapses may rarely find themselves in Twilight in the material realm. I'd assume leaving the Dreaming Roads in dream form and portaling to the material realm would work similarly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2